			"to": "western-civ/royal-society",
			"why": "The Royal Society kept its own cabinet of rarities at Gresham College, cataloged in 1681 by Nehemiah Grew, Oldenburg's successor as secretary, who asked of Worm's unicorn-horn trials whether the dogs might have lived without the horn."
		},
		{
			"to": "biology/gesner",
			"why": "Gessner reported the pigeon test of unicorn horn and left it \"to the rich\"; Worm and an apothecary ran it on pigeons and kittens in 1636, with scrapings of a narwhal's tusk."
		}
	],
